			],
			"Message": "chore(Maintain): Swap emoji from wrench to flexed bicep in Architecture.md header\n\nReplace the 🔧 (wrench) emoji with 💪🏻 (flexed bicep) in the table header and page title of Architecture.md to better convey the \"build system and CI/CD toolkit\" identity of Maintain rather than a repair/tooling connotation.\n\nSingle cosmetic change across two locations in the file with no semantic impact on content or structure.",
			"SHA": "79baf770921b53f6a99f27d8ce6c22429fc18df0"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-07-08T16:28:22Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				143,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Maintain): Add funding acknowledgement section with grant details\n\nExpand the Funding & Acknowledgements section in README.md with a narrative paragraph describing Land as an NLnet NGI0 Commons Fund open-source endeavor, and add a structured table header row identifying Land, PlayForm, NLnet, and NGI0 Commons Fund. Normalize all GitHub blob links to tree links for consistency with the existing link style.\n\n- Insert introductory paragraph before the funding acknowledgement block\n- Add `<thead>` with organization-name headers above the existing logo row\n- Lowercase the Land website URL to match the PlayForm and NLnet URL style\n- Switch LICENSE and CHANGELOG anchor links from `/blob/` to `/tree/`\n- Reword the Changelog paragraph to include an invitation tone\n- Remove the separate PlayForm steward sentence, folding the context into the NLnet project page reference\n\nAll changes are cosmetic documentation improvements with no functional impact.",
			"SHA": "83ae13bd6fa18ce7b32fbac074b1544aad9fa141"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-07-08T16:09:53Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				143,
				1
			],
			"Message": "style(Maintain): Remove extraneous en-space separators from badges and prose\n\nClean up inconsistent whitespace in README.md badge lines and narrative text. The en-space separators (&#x2001;) between badge images and version labels in the hero section were visually redundant with natural spacing; remove them for cleaner rendering. Also strip trailing en-space markers from bullet-point descriptions for \".vscode/land-config.json\" and \"Development Runner with Hot-Reload\" and the target-triple paragraph in the Overview.\n\nAdditionally fix an extraneous en-space after the \"System Architecture\" heading, and normalize the Land emoji en-space usage throughout the integration table and Land project section — removing orphaned en-spaces that appeared after closing emoji spans with no following text.\n\nAll changes are cosmetic whitespace normalization with no semantic impact on content or markup structure.",
			"SHA": "8ed5d6677d06dc17fd70e2c7038898e70bec360e"
		}
	],
